          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सजना (sajnā) is probably related to Hindi sājnā, \"to be prepared\", which CDIAL files under Sanskrit sajjyatē, \"is equipped, is prepared\" (CDIAL 13093); CDIAL does not list sajnā itself; it is the intransitive partner of sajānā, \"to decorate\"."
            }
          ]
